<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.4: Dividing Polynomial Functions and the Remainder Theorem</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01620</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.4: Dividing Polynomial Functions and the Remainder Theorem</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5e609ce2-629d-40e7-87fc-a207e1a10897</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Divide the polynomial functions. Find the quotient value.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2-5x-24\) </para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-8\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2-15x+54\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-6\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(f(x)=x^2+2x-3\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <para>\((\frac{f}{g})(x)=x-1\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->
<para>The Remainder Theorem states that if a polynomial function \(f(x)\) is divided by \(x-c\), then the remainder is \(f(c)\). This means we can always compare the remainder by finding \(f(c)\) when the divisor is written in the form \(x-c\).</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="6ebd9efc-82d3-4dc9-8291-3e4d1a8337a0" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="1354241e-b60c-45b8-951b-099be0a8eba8" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="6">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder when \(f(x)=x^3-7x+12\) is divided by \(x + 3\).</para>
        <para> Enter the remainder here.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The remainder is 6</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise> 
  <!--Interaction End -->
  <exercise data-content-id="53f4a375-e2b9-4945-a16f-9fc9e4fd3361" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="12">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder when \(f(x)=2x^3-6x-24\) is divided by \(x - 3\).</para>
      <para> Enter the remainder here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The remainder is 12</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
</section>
